# CODEOWNERS — https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# One maintainer today, so this file's job is not to divide review work. It is to
# make the paths that carry the most risk impossible to change without the owner
# being asked, and to survive the day a second maintainer arrives.
#
# Every rule below is a real ownership boundary, not a placeholder: if you add a
# maintainer, add them to the rule that covers what they maintain.

# Everything, by default.
*                           @drsamonline

# The grammar is the contract every other layer is checked against. A change here
# changes the language, so it needs the owner even if the diff is one line.
/grammar/                   @drsamonline
/tools/grammar-check.py     @drsamonline

# Anything that emits code, and anything a program is linked against.
/compiler/src/backend/      @drsamonline
/backends/                  @drsamonline
/runtime/                   @drsamonline

# The pipeline the whole project rests on.
/compiler/src/lexer/        @drsamonline
/compiler/src/parser/       @drsamonline
/compiler/src/sema/         @drsamonline
/compiler/src/lowerer/      @drsamonline
/crates/nova-common/src/sir/ @drsamonline

# Provenance, release and supply chain.
/.github/workflows/         @drsamonline
/MANIFEST.json              @drsamonline
/Cargo.lock                 @drsamonline
/NOTICE                     @drsamonline
/SECURITY.md                @drsamonline
/LICENSE                    @drsamonline

# The status documents. `DEV_PLAN.md` is the source of truth for what is done, so
# a change to it is a change to the project's claims about itself.
/DEV_PLAN.md                @drsamonline
/CHANGELOG.md               @drsamonline
/README.md                  @drsamonline
